## Structured Logging

```java
// ✅ Use key-value pairs for structured logging
import static net.logstash.logback.argument.StructuredArguments.kv;

private static final Logger log = LoggerFactory.getLogger(ExecutionService.class);

public void startExecution(ExecutionId executionId) {
    log.info("Starting execution", 
        kv("executionId", executionId),
        kv("tenantId", TenantContext.current()));
    
    try {
        // ...
        log.info("Execution started successfully",
            kv("executionId", executionId),
            kv("durationMs", timer.elapsed()));
    } catch (Exception e) {
        log.error("Failed to start execution",
            kv("executionId", executionId),
            kv("error", e.getMessage()),
            e);  // Include exception for stack trace
        throw e;
    }
}

// ❌ Never use string concatenation
log.info("Starting execution " + executionId);  // Wrong

// ❌ Never log sensitive data
log.info("User logged in", kv("password", password));  // NEVER
```

## Log Levels

| Level | When to Use | Example |
|-------|-------------|---------|
| ERROR | Requires immediate attention | Database connection failed |
| WARN | Unexpected but handled | Retry attempt, deprecation |
| INFO | Business events | Execution started, completed |
| DEBUG | Debugging info | Method entry/exit, values |
| TRACE | Very detailed | Loop iterations, all data |

## Metrics with Micrometer

```java
@Component
public class ExecutionMetrics {
    private final Counter executionsStarted;
    private final Counter executionsFailed;
    private final Timer executionDuration;
    private final Gauge activeExecutions;
    
    public ExecutionMetrics(MeterRegistry registry) {
        this.executionsStarted = Counter.builder("pravah.executions.started")
            .description("Number of executions started")
            .tag("service", "execution-service")
            .register(registry);
        
        this.executionsFailed = Counter.builder("pravah.executions.failed")
            .description("Number of executions failed")
            .tag("service", "execution-service")
            .register(registry);
        
        this.executionDuration = Timer.builder("pravah.executions.duration")
            .description("Execution duration")
            .publishPercentiles(0.5, 0.95, 0.99)
            .register(registry);
    }
    
    public void recordExecutionStarted() {
        executionsStarted.increment();
    }
    
    public void recordExecutionCompleted(Duration duration, boolean success) {
        executionDuration.record(duration);
        if (!success) executionsFailed.increment();
    }
}
```

## Distributed Tracing

```java
// ✅ Traces propagate automatically with Spring Boot + OTel
// Add custom spans for important operations

@Service
public class ExecutionService {
    private final Tracer tracer;
    
    public Execution startExecution(StartExecutionCommand cmd) {
        Span span = tracer.spanBuilder("startExecution")
            .setAttribute("execution.id", cmd.executionId().toString())
            .setAttribute("pipeline.id", cmd.pipelineId().toString())
            .startSpan();
        
        try (Scope scope = span.makeCurrent()) {
            // Business logic here
            span.addEvent("validation_complete");
            
            var execution = createExecution(cmd);
            
            span.addEvent("execution_created");
            span.setStatus(StatusCode.OK);
            
            return execution;
        } catch (Exception e) {
            span.setStatus(StatusCode.ERROR, e.getMessage());
            span.recordException(e);
            throw e;
        } finally {
            span.end();
        }
    }
}
```

## Health Checks

```java
@Component
public class DatabaseHealthIndicator implements HealthIndicator {
    private final DataSource dataSource;
    
    @Override
    public Health health() {
        try (Connection conn = dataSource.getConnection()) {
            conn.createStatement().execute("SELECT 1");
            return Health.up()
                .withDetail("database", "PostgreSQL")
                .build();
        } catch (SQLException e) {
            return Health.down()
                .withDetail("error", e.getMessage())
                .build();
        }
    }
}

// Kubernetes probes
// /actuator/health/liveness  → App is running
// /actuator/health/readiness → App can accept traffic
```

## Alerting Context

When errors occur, include enough context for debugging:

```java
log.error("Job execution failed",
    kv("jobId", jobId),
    kv("executionId", executionId),
    kv("pipelineId", pipelineId),
    kv("tenantId", tenantId),
    kv("runnerId", runnerId),
    kv("attempt", attempt),
    kv("errorType", e.getClass().getSimpleName()),
    kv("errorMessage", e.getMessage()),
    e);
```
